IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- INSTRUMENT: Broadcasting (Class Licence) Notification (G.N. No. S 306/1996; N 1, 2004 Revised Edition, amended to S 478/2020), made under s 9 of the Act.
-- Deposit: ../../../broadcasting-class-licence-notification-1996/registers/source-bundle/BA1994-N1.txt (lawplain's rendering, line-broken by hand).
-- THE SCHEDULE (the conditions of the class licence, para 4) IS NOT IN THE TEXT SERVED: no condition of this class licence is encoded (coverage row "source not obtained").
-- Dated: the window of the Notification as deposited. NOTHING outside it.

§ `Paragraph 2: Definitions`

-- src:6 | “Internet Content Provider” means —
-- src:7 | ( a ) any individual in Singapore who provides any programme, for business, political or religious purposes, on the World Wide Web through the Internet; or
-- src:8 | ( b ) any corporation or group of individuals (including any association, business, club, company, society, organisation or partnership, whether registrable or incorporated under the laws of Singapore or not) who provides any programme on the World Wide Web through the Internet, and includes any web publisher and any web server administrator;
@ref para 2 "Internet Content Provider" (src:6-8)
GIVEN `it is an individual in Singapore who provides a programme, for business, political or religious purposes, on the World Wide Web through the Internet` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a corporation or group of individuals (including an association, business, club, company, society, organisation or partnership, whether registrable or incorporated under the laws of Singapore or not) who provides a programme on the World Wide Web through the Internet, including a web publisher or web server administrator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 the person is an Internet Content Provider` MEANS
    `it is an individual in Singapore who provides a programme, for business, political or religious purposes, on the World Wide Web through the Internet`
    OR `it is a corporation or group of individuals (including an association, business, club, company, society, organisation or partnership, whether registrable or incorporated under the laws of Singapore or not) who provides a programme on the World Wide Web through the Internet, including a web publisher or web server administrator`

-- src:13 | “Localised Internet Service Reseller” means a person —
-- src:14 | ( a ) who obtains Internet access from an Internet Access Service Provider or from a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller;
-- src:15 | ( b ) who provides Internet services obtained from the Internet Access Service Provider, or the Non- localised Internet Service Reseller, to all or part of the public; and
-- src:16 | ( c ) whose Internet services are available for reception only within a single building, dwelling-house, hospital, educational institution, residential, commercial or industrial complex, or any other single temporary or permanent structure,
-- src:17 | but does not include a person who provides Internet services to that person’s own employees for use solely within that person’s firm or corporation;
@ref para 2 "Localised Internet Service Reseller" (src:13-17)
GIVEN `it obtains Internet access from an Internet Access Service Provider or from a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides the Internet services so obtained to all or part of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its Internet services are available for reception only within a single building, dwelling-house, hospital, educational institution, residential, commercial or industrial complex, or other single temporary or permanent structure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides Internet services to its own employees for use solely within its firm or corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 the person is a Localised Internet Service Reseller` MEANS
    `it obtains Internet access from an Internet Access Service Provider or from a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller`
    AND `it provides the Internet services so obtained to all or part of the public`
    AND `its Internet services are available for reception only within a single building, dwelling-house, hospital, educational institution, residential, commercial or industrial complex, or other single temporary or permanent structure`
    AND (NOT `it provides Internet services to its own employees for use solely within its firm or corporation`)

-- src:18 | “Non-localised Internet Service Reseller” means a person who —
-- src:19 | ( a ) obtains Internet access from an Internet Access Service Provider; and
-- src:20 | ( b ) provides Internet services obtained from the Internet Access Service Provider to all or part of the public by leased telecommunication lines, integrated services digital networks, modems or by any other wired or wireless means,
-- src:21 | but does not include a person who provides Internet services to that person’s own employees for use solely within that person’s firm or corporation;
@ref para 2 "Non-localised Internet Service Reseller" (src:18-21)
GIVEN `it obtains Internet access from an Internet Access Service Provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides the Internet services so obtained to all or part of the public by leased telecommunication lines, integrated services digital networks, modems or any other wired or wireless means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it provides Internet services to its own employees for use solely within its firm or corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 the person is a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller` MEANS
    `it obtains Internet access from an Internet Access Service Provider`
    AND `it provides the Internet services so obtained to all or part of the public by leased telecommunication lines, integrated services digital networks, modems or any other wired or wireless means`
    AND (NOT `it provides Internet services to its own employees for use solely within its firm or corporation`)

-- src:9 | “Internet Service Provider” means any of the following persons:
-- src:10 | ( a ) an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act (Cap. 323);
-- src:11 | ( b ) a Localised Internet Service Reseller; or
-- src:12 | ( c ) a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller;
@ref para 2 "Internet Service Provider" (src:9-12)
GIVEN `it is an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Localised Internet Service Reseller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 the person is an Internet Service Provider` MEANS
    `it is an Internet Access Service Provider licensed under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act` OR `it is a Localised Internet Service Reseller` OR `it is a Non-localised Internet Service Reseller`

-- src:22 | “VAN computer on-line service” means a computer on-line service that is licensed as a Value Added Network service under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act.
@ref para 2 "VAN computer on-line service" (src:22)
GIVEN `it is a computer on-line service licensed as a Value Added Network service under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 2 the service is a VAN computer on-line service` MEANS
    `it is a computer on-line service licensed as a Value Added Network service under section 5 of the Telecommunications Act`

§ `Paragraph 3: Licensable broadcasting services subject to class licence`

-- src:24 | 3. The provision of the following licensable broadcasting services are subject to a class licence, except a computer on-line service provided on or after such date as the Authority specifies in a notice given to the provider of the service under paragraph 3A:
-- src:25 | ( a ) audiotext services;
-- src:26 | ( b ) videotext services;
-- src:27 | ( c ) teletext services;
-- src:28 | ( d ) broadcast data services;
-- src:29 | ( e ) VAN computer on-line services; and
-- src:30 | ( f ) computer on-line services that are provided by Internet Content Providers and Internet Service Providers.
@ref para 3 (a) to (f) (src:24-30)
-- The class licence applies to the provision of the listed services, EXCEPT a computer on-line service provided on or after the date the Authority
-- specifies in a notice given under para 3A. The Act's s 8(1) is then met by the class licence.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A MAYBE `Second Schedule service`
      `it is a VAN computer on-line service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a computer on-line service provided by an Internet Content Provider or an Internet Service Provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has given the provider a notice under paragraph 3A(1) specifying a date, and the date has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3 the provision of the service is subject to the class licence, on` MEANS
    IF `the Class Licence Notification as deposited is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (CONSIDER s
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST x THEN
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN `audiotext services` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `videotext services` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `teletext services` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `broadcast data services` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `computer online services` THEN (`it is a VAN computer on-line service` OR `it is a computer on-line service provided by an Internet Content Provider or an Internet Service Provider`) AND (NOT `the Authority has given the provider a notice under paragraph 3A(1) specifying a date, and the date has been reached`)
            OTHERWISE FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Paragraph 3A: Exclusion from class licence`

-- src:33 | 3A. —(1) A notice may be given by the Authority to any person who provides a computer on-line service in or from Singapore, whether for payment or free, and whether at regular intervals or otherwise —
-- src:34 | ( a ) that is accessed from at least 50,000 different Internet protocol addresses in Singapore per month on average, over any period of 2 consecutive months; and
-- src:35 | ( b ) that contains at least one Singapore news programme per week on average, over the same period of 2 consecutive months referred to in sub-paragraph ( a ),
@ref para 3A(1)(a) and (b) (src:33-35)
GIVEN `the service is accessed from at least 50,000 different Internet protocol addresses in Singapore per month on average, over a period of 2 consecutive months` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service contains at least one Singapore news programme per week on average, over the same period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3A(1) a notice may be given by the Authority to the provider` MEANS
    `the service is accessed from at least 50,000 different Internet protocol addresses in Singapore per month on average, over a period of 2 consecutive months`
    AND `the service contains at least one Singapore news programme per week on average, over the same period`

-- src:36 | and that notice shall not cease to have effect by reason only that the computer on-line service concerned ceases subsequently to satisfy sub-paragraph ( a ) or ( b ) during the validity of any broadcasting licence under section 8 of the Act relating to that service.
@ref para 3A(1) (the notice does not cease to have effect) (src:36)
GIVEN `a notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the service ceases subsequently to satisfy sub-paragraph (a) or (b) during the validity of a broadcasting licence under section 8 relating to the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3A(1) the notice has ceased to have effect by reason only of that` MEANS
    IF `a notice was given` AND `the service ceases subsequently to satisfy sub-paragraph (a) or (b) during the validity of a broadcasting licence under section 8 relating to the service` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:37 | (2) For the purposes of reckoning access and content under sub-paragraph (1)( a ) and ( b ) —
-- src:38 | ( a ) where a computer on-line service is provided by a web site with a domain and one or more sub-domains, all sub-domains shall be regarded as part of the domain of the web site; and
-- src:39 | ( b ) where a computer on-line service is provided by a web site in or from Singapore (referred to in this sub-paragraph as the original web site) which is duplicated on or transferred to one or more other web sites in or from Singapore (referred to in this sub-paragraph as the mirrored web site), all mirrored web sites shall be regarded as part of the original web site.
@ref para 3A(2) (src:37-39)
GIVEN `the web site has a domain and one or more sub-domains` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3A(2)(a) all sub-domains are regarded as part of the domain of the web site` MEANS
    IF `the web site has a domain and one or more sub-domains` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:39 | ( b ) where a computer on-line service is provided by a web site in or from Singapore (referred to in this sub-paragraph as the original web site) which is duplicated on or transferred to one or more other web sites in or from Singapore (referred to in this sub-paragraph as the mirrored web site), all mirrored web sites shall be regarded as part of the original web site.
@ref para 3A(2)(b) (src:39)
GIVEN `the original web site in or from Singapore is duplicated on or transferred to other web sites in or from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3A(2)(b) all mirrored web sites are regarded as part of the original web site` MEANS
    IF `the original web site in or from Singapore is duplicated on or transferred to other web sites in or from Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:40 | (3) In this paragraph, “Singapore news programme” means any programme (whether or not the programme is presenter-based and whether or not the programme is provided by a third party) containing any news, intelligence, report of occurrence, or any matter of public interest, about any social, economic, political, cultural, artistic, sporting, scientific or any other aspect of Singapore in any language (whether paid or free and whether at regular intervals or otherwise) but does not include any programme produced by or on behalf of the Government.
@ref para 3A(3) "Singapore news programme" (src:40)
GIVEN `it contains news, intelligence, report of occurrence, or any matter of public interest, about an aspect of Singapore in any language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was produced by or on behalf of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3A(3) the programme is a Singapore news programme` MEANS
    `it contains news, intelligence, report of occurrence, or any matter of public interest, about an aspect of Singapore in any language` AND (NOT `it was produced by or on behalf of the Government`)

-- src:41 | (4) This Notification also does not apply to or in relation to a person who is a class licensee by virtue of the Broadcasting (Class Licence — Broadcasting to Digital Display Panels) Notification 2020 (G.N. No. S 477/2020).
@ref para 3A(4) (src:41)
GIVEN `the person is a class licensee by virtue of the Broadcasting (Class Licence -- Broadcasting to Digital Display Panels) Notification 2020` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 3A(4) this Notification does not apply to or in relation to the person` MEANS
    `the person is a class licensee by virtue of the Broadcasting (Class Licence -- Broadcasting to Digital Display Panels) Notification 2020`

§ `Paragraphs 4 and 5: Conditions of class licence; application of conditions`

-- src:45 | 4. The conditions of the class licence referred to in paragraph 3 are set out in the Schedule.
@ref para 4 (src:45)
-- The conditions are in the Schedule, which the text served does not carry: nothing here says what any condition is.
GIVEN `the Schedule's conditions are known` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 4 the conditions of the class licence are set out in the Schedule` MEANS
    IF `the Schedule's conditions are known` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:47 | 5. The conditions of the class licence set out in the Schedule apply to the provision of any licensable broadcasting service that is subject to a class licence where the service is available or continues to be provided after 15th July 1996 notwithstanding that the service was available or first provided before 15th July 1996.
@ref para 5 (src:47)
GIVEN `the service is available or continues to be provided after 15 July 1996` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`N 1 para 5 the conditions of the class licence apply to the service, even if it was available or first provided before 15 July 1996` MEANS
    IF `the service is available or continues to be provided after 15 July 1996` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
